+7 Conclusion
+
+The repository provides a modular starting point for SafeVoice, but the code review identifies
+concrete inconsistencies between the CDM, form, cleaner and RDF mapping. The datatype lookup
+does not match the current CDM labels, required-field rules are hard-coded inconsistently, and some
+RDF placeholders do not match the flattened input columns. Several collected fields, including the
+Source ID, never reach the RDF graph, and untouched form fields are submitted with default values.
+The current Source ID mechanism is not authentication, the ingestion function does not use Source
+ID to select an isolated AllegroGraph repository or graph context, and a Source ID containing path
+characters can place generated files outside the intended directories. The application also retains
+raw JSON locally, including original location precision, and the Manage Reports page displays that
+archive, even though the cleaned DataFrame rounds selected coordinates.
+
+    The proposed work addresses these findings across all four HDS windows. The immediate
+priorities are a consistent schema contract, tested RDF mapping, a topic-based narrative-first
+workflow and identity-based access control. Document storage, organisational SSO and FDP
+registration are important parts of the longer-term target architecture, but depend on infrastructure
+and decisions that are not currently confirmed. This distinction keeps the technical plan evidence-
+based and realistic.
+
